# Destow gateway - the single entry point. Every request enters here and is
# proxied to the API. Caddy passes WebSocket upgrades through transparently,
# so REST and Socket.io both work.
#
# Local: listens on :80 (mapped to host :3000). No TLS locally.
# Prod:  replace ":80" with "api.destow.com" and Caddy auto-provisions HTTPS.
#
# Auth model: the API is authoritative for auth (it owns the Redis revocation
# denylist), so the gateway only proxies. Caddy forwards Authorization untouched
# and sets X-Forwarded-For, which the API trusts (app.set('trust proxy', 1)) to
# read the real client IP for rate limiting and session records.
#
# Optional future hardening: with EdDSA tokens, a caddy-jwt plugin can reject
# unsigned/expired tokens at the edge using /.well-known/jwks.json as a COARSE
# pre-filter - the API still does the authoritative denylist check.
:80 {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy api:3000
}
